# Build output. This is the 30 GB: Cargo rebuilds every byte of it from source.
/target/

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This workspace ships a binary, and a
# committed lock file is what makes a build reproducible for everyone else.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development-only probes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These three were written to *tune* the app, not to test it. Each needs a real,
# curated music collection to say anything useful, each prints that collection
# to stdout, and each answered its question once — the answers are now constants
# in the source. They stay out of the repository because a probe you cannot run
# without someone else's music library is not much use to a contributor, and
# because pasting their output into a bug report leaks what you listen to.
#
# The six examples that remain all either assert something or help diagnose a
# real problem; see the README.
/crates/mp-core/examples/accent_probe.rs
/crates/mp-core/examples/discover_probe.rs
/crates/mp-audio/examples/sound_probe.rs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A library or settings file must never travel with the source. The app keeps
# its own under %APPDATA%/Resonance, but these appear in the repository root if
# you run a portable build or a probe from here.
/Resonance-data/
resonance.portable
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
config.v*.bak.toml

# Probe output.
*.png
*.html
!/docs/**

# Editors and OS clutter.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
